@startuml 08a_container_layout
!include _style.puml
title File formats (a) - common container used by .ascii, .aanim and .aspr  (all integers LITTLE-ENDIAN)

class "ContainerHeader  (fixed 20 bytes)" as Header <<binary>> {
  offset 0  | size 4 | magic            : [u8;4]   "ASCI" (.ascii) / "AANM" (.aanim) / "ASPR" (.aspr)
  offset 4  | size 2 | version          : u16      = 1
  offset 6  | size 2 | flags            : u16      bit0 = payload is zstd-compressed, bits 1..15 MUST be 0
  offset 8  | size 4 | uncompressed_len : u32      length of the payload after decompression
  offset 12 | size 4 | stored_len       : u32      number of bytes that follow the header
  offset 16 | size 4 | crc32            : u32      CRC-32 (IEEE, crc32fast) of the UNCOMPRESSED payload
}

class "Payload  (stored_len bytes)" as Payload <<binary>> {
  zstd level 3 stream when flags.bit0 = 1
  raw bytes when flags.bit0 = 0 (stored_len == uncompressed_len)
}

class "File on disk" as File <<binary>>

File *-- "1  @0" Header
File *-- "1  @20" Payload

note right of File
  Extension <-> magic <-> payload content
  .ascii : "ASCI" : CanvasHeader + 1 FlatFrameBlock                    ONE flattened image (layers merged, hidden layers left out)
  .aanim : "AANM" : CanvasHeader + AnimHeader + N FlatFrameBlock       flattened animation
  .aspr  : "ASPR" : CanvasHeader + ProjectMeta + ProjectHeader + N LayeredFrameBlock     the project, with all layers
  (payload layouts: diagram 08b, worked examples: 08c flat, 08d layered)
  "Export as ASCII image sequence" writes N separate .ascii files, one per frame - there is no extra container for it.
  Version stays 1: the layouts in this pack replace the earlier draft (single-layer cells). If you already wrote files with the old draft layout, bump the version to 2.
end note

note bottom of Header
  Writing (ContainerCodec::wrap)
  1. crc = crc32(payload).  2. c = zstd(payload, level 3).
  3. if c.len() < payload.len(): flags = 1, body = c  else: flags = 0, body = payload.
  4. emit header (stored_len = body.len()), then body.
  Payload larger than 512 MiB -> Err(TooLarge) before anything is written.

  Reading (ContainerCodec::unwrap) - checks in THIS order, first failure wins
  1. bytes.len() >= 20                        else Truncated
  2. magic == expected magic of the requested FileKind   else BadMagic
  3. version <= 1                              else UnsupportedVersion(version)   (version 0 is also rejected)
  4. flags & 0xFFFE == 0                       else ReservedFlags(flags)
  5. bytes.len() == 20 + stored_len            else Truncated (shorter) / LengthMismatch (longer)
  6. if bit0: payload = zstd::decode (max output = uncompressed_len, refuse to exceed it)  else payload = body
  7. payload.len() == uncompressed_len         else LengthMismatch
  8. crc32(payload) == crc32 field             else CrcMismatch
  Maximum accepted uncompressed_len = 512 MiB (guards against decompression bombs).
end note

@enduml

@startuml 08b_payload_layouts
!include _style.puml
title File formats (b) - payload layouts (all integers LITTLE-ENDIAN, strings = u16 byte-length + UTF-8 bytes, no terminator)

class "CanvasHeader  (8 + font_name bytes)" as CanvasHeader <<binary>> {
  cols      : u16   1..=1024   (default 240)
  rows      : u16   1..=1024   (default 72)
  cell_w    : u8    1..=64     (default 8)
  cell_h    : u8    1..=64     (default 15)
  font_name : string  0..=256 bytes   (e.g. "default")
}

class "FlatFrameBlock  (3 + 12 * cols * rows bytes)  - .ascii and .aanim" as FlatFrameBlock <<binary>> {
  background : [u8;3]              RGB of the frame background colour (opaque, lies UNDER the image)
  glyph_plane: [u32; cols*rows]    Unicode scalar value per cell of the flattened image, row-major (index = row*cols + col). U+0020 = no character
  ink_plane  : [u8;4 * cols*rows]  R,G,B,A per cell: the mixed colour of the glyph (meaningless where the glyph is U+0020)
  fill_plane : [u8;4 * cols*rows]  R,G,B,A per cell: the mixed background colour. A = 0 means "nothing here" (the frame background shows)
}

class "FrameHeader  (7 bytes)  - .aspr only" as FrameHeader <<binary>> {
  background   : [u8;3]   RGB of the frame background colour
  active_layer : u16      index of the layer the tools edit, < layer_count (0 = bottom layer)
  layer_count  : u16      1..=64
}

class "LayerBlock  (4 + name bytes + 12 * cols * rows)  - .aspr only" as LayerBlock <<binary>> {
  name        : string   0..=256 bytes  (1..=64 characters in the UI)
  flags       : u8       bit0 = visible, bits 1..7 MUST be 0
  opacity     : u8       0..=255  (255 = opaque layer)
  glyph_plane : [u32; cols*rows]     foreground plane: Unicode scalar per cell (U+0020 = no character)
  ink_plane   : [u8;4 * cols*rows]   foreground plane: R,G,B,A of the glyph
  fill_plane  : [u8;4 * cols*rows]   background plane: R,G,B,A of the cell fill (A = 0 = nothing)
}

class "LayeredFrameBlock  - .aspr only" as LayeredFrameBlock <<binary>>

class "AnimHeader  (8 bytes)  - .aanim only" as AnimHeader <<binary>> {
  fps         : u8     1..=60
  flags       : u8     bit0 = loop, bits 1..7 MUST be 0
  reserved    : u16    MUST be 0
  frame_count : u32    1..=10000
}

class "ProjectMeta  - .aspr only" as ProjectMeta <<binary>> {
  name        : string   1..=1024 bytes
  created_at  : i64      Unix seconds (UTC)
  modified_at : i64      Unix seconds (UTC)
  app_version : string   0..=64 bytes   (e.g. "0.1.0")
}

class "ProjectHeader  (12 bytes)  - .aspr only" as ProjectHeader <<binary>> {
  fps            : u8    1..=60
  flags          : u8    bit0 = loop, bits 1..7 MUST be 0
  reserved       : u16   MUST be 0
  selected_index : u32   < frame_count
  frame_count    : u32   1..=10000
}

class ".ascii payload" as AsciiPayload <<binary>>
class ".aanim payload" as AanimPayload <<binary>>
class ".aspr payload"  as AsprPayload  <<binary>>

AsciiPayload *-- "1 (1st)" CanvasHeader
AsciiPayload *-- "1 (2nd)" FlatFrameBlock

AanimPayload *-- "1 (1st)" CanvasHeader
AanimPayload *-- "1 (2nd)" AnimHeader
AanimPayload *-- "frame_count (3rd..)" FlatFrameBlock

AsprPayload *-- "1 (1st)" CanvasHeader
AsprPayload *-- "1 (2nd)" ProjectMeta
AsprPayload *-- "1 (3rd)" ProjectHeader
AsprPayload *-- "frame_count (4th..)" LayeredFrameBlock

LayeredFrameBlock *-- "1 (1st)" FrameHeader
LayeredFrameBlock *-- "layer_count (2nd.., bottom layer first)" LayerBlock

note bottom of FlatFrameBlock
  Size example for the default canvas (240 x 72 = 17 280 cells):
  3 + 17280*4 (glyph) + 17280*4 (ink) + 17280*4 (fill) = 207 363 bytes per frame, before zstd.
  Planes are stored separately (not interleaved per cell) because blank areas then compress to almost nothing.
  The flattened colours are what Compositor::flatten produced (diagram 20c); the frame background is stored separately and NOT merged into fill_plane.

  Decoding a FlatFrameBlock (FlatFrameBlockCodec::read)
  - needs exactly 3 + 12*cols*rows bytes, otherwise Truncated.
  - glyph value that is not a valid Unicode scalar (surrogates, > 0x10FFFF) -> replaced by U+FFFD (lenient, no error).
  - any alpha value 0..=255 is valid. Entries with A = 0 are normalised to (0,0,0,0), a U+0020 glyph forces its ink entry to (0,0,0,0).
  - Writing: the writer already emits normalised values, so identical images always produce identical bytes.
end note

note bottom of LayerBlock
  Size example for the default canvas: one layer named "Layer 1" = 2 + 7 + 2 + 12*17280 = 207 371 bytes, plus 7 bytes of FrameHeader per frame
  (a frame with one layer = 207 378 bytes before zstd). Every extra layer costs about the same, so a blank layer is cheap only AFTER zstd.

  Decoding a LayeredFrameBlock (LayeredFrameBlockCodec::read)
  - FrameHeader: layer_count 1..=64 and active_layer < layer_count, otherwise InvalidField("layer_count" / "active_layer", range text).
  - LayerBlock: flags bits 1..7 set -> InvalidField("layer.flags", "reserved bits set"). name must be valid UTF-8 (else InvalidField("layer.name", ..));
    an empty name becomes "Layer <n>". Glyph / alpha rules are the same as in the FlatFrameBlock.
  - LayerIds are NOT stored: after loading, the layers of every frame receive ids 1..=layer_count (bottom to top) and frame.next_layer_id = layer_count + 1.
  - FrameIds are NOT stored: frames receive ids 1..=N in order and project.next_frame_id = N + 1. Frame.revision is not stored (starts at 0).
  - The project canvas size comes from the CanvasHeader, so a project whose canvas was grown by an import reopens with the grown size.
end note

note bottom of ProjectHeader
  Decoding rules (AsprCodec::decode)
  - After the last LayeredFrameBlock there must be 0 remaining bytes, otherwise InvalidField("payload", "trailing bytes").
  - cols/rows/cell_w/cell_h/fps/frame_count/selected_index outside the ranges above -> InvalidField(<n>, <range text>).
  - reserved fields != 0 or reserved flag bits set -> InvalidField(<n>, "reserved bits set").
  - Encoding (AsprCodec::encode): meta.name must be 1..=1024 bytes (the New Project modal already limits it to 64 chars).
    The encoded payload must stay <= 512 MiB, otherwise Err(TooLarge).
  AanimCodec::decode applies the same rules without ProjectMeta / selected_index (the loaded timeline selects frame 0), reading FlatFrameBlocks.
  AsciiCodec::decode: the single FlatFrameBlock is returned as AsciiImage.frame (a FlatFrame, not a layered Frame).
end note

@enduml

@startuml 08c_test_vector
!include _style.puml
title File formats (c) - worked example (unit-test vector): a 2 x 1 cell .ascii file, 62 bytes, stored uncompressed

legend top right
  Image content (flattened): cell 0 = 'H' white (opaque) on nothing (fill transparent).  cell 1 = 'i' red (opaque) on blue at alpha 0x80 (50 %).
  Frame background #000000. Canvas 2 x 1, cell 8 x 15, font_name "default".
  The payload (42 bytes) zstd-compresses to 51 bytes (larger), so the writer stores it RAW: flags = 0, stored_len = 42.
end legend

map "ContainerHeader  (offset 0, 20 bytes)" as H {
  magic => 41 53 43 49   ("ASCI")
  version => 01 00
  flags => 00 00
  uncompressed_len => 2A 00 00 00   (42)
  stored_len => 2A 00 00 00   (42)
  crc32 => FE 21 71 A0   (0xA07121FE)
}

map "CanvasHeader  (offset 20, 15 bytes)" as C {
  cols => 02 00
  rows => 01 00
  cell_w => 08
  cell_h => 0F
  font_name => 07 00 + 64 65 66 61 75 6C 74   ("default")
}

map "FlatFrameBlock  (offset 35, 27 bytes)" as F {
  background => 00 00 00
  glyph_plane => 48 00 00 00 | 69 00 00 00   ('H', 'i')
  ink_plane => FF FF FF FF | FF 00 00 FF   (white opaque | red opaque)
  fill_plane => 00 00 00 00 | 00 00 FF 80   (nothing | blue, alpha 0x80)
}

H -[hidden]down-> C
C -[hidden]down-> F

note bottom of F
  Full file (62 bytes):
  41 53 43 49 01 00 00 00 2A 00 00 00 2A 00 00 00 FE 21 71 A0
  02 00 01 00 08 0F 07 00 64 65 66 61 75 6C 74
  00 00 00  48 00 00 00 69 00 00 00  FF FF FF FF FF 00 00 FF  00 00 00 00 00 00 FF 80
  A test must assert: encode(image) == these 62 bytes, and decode(these 62 bytes) == image.
end note

@enduml

@startuml 08d_test_vector_layered
!include _style.puml
title File formats (d) - worked example (unit-test vector): ONE LayeredFrameBlock of an .aspr, 2 x 1 cells, 2 layers, 70 bytes

legend top right
  Frame background #101020, active layer = 1 (the top one), 2 layers (bottom first).
  Layer 0 "base": visible, opacity 255. cells: 'H' white on nothing | 'i' red on blue at alpha 0x80.
  Layer 1 "top": HIDDEN, opacity 0x80. cells: no character | 'X' green (opaque). Fill plane empty.
  This is the block only (it sits after the ProjectHeader inside an .aspr payload). Canvas 2 x 1.
  Flattening this frame must give the cells of diagram 08c, because the hidden layer is skipped.
end legend

map "FrameHeader  (offset 0, 7 bytes)" as FH {
  background => 10 10 20
  active_layer => 01 00
  layer_count => 02 00
}

map "LayerBlock 0  (offset 7, 32 bytes)" as L0 {
  name => 04 00 + 62 61 73 65   ("base")
  flags => 01   (visible)
  opacity => FF
  glyph_plane => 48 00 00 00 | 69 00 00 00   ('H', 'i')
  ink_plane => FF FF FF FF | FF 00 00 FF
  fill_plane => 00 00 00 00 | 00 00 FF 80
}

map "LayerBlock 1  (offset 39, 31 bytes)" as L1 {
  name => 03 00 + 74 6F 70   ("top")
  flags => 00   (hidden)
  opacity => 80
  glyph_plane => 20 00 00 00 | 58 00 00 00   (' ', 'X')
  ink_plane => 00 00 00 00 | 00 FF 00 FF   (empty | green opaque)
  fill_plane => 00 00 00 00 | 00 00 00 00
}

FH -[hidden]down-> L0
L0 -[hidden]down-> L1

note bottom of L1
  Full block (70 bytes):
  10 10 20 01 00 02 00
  04 00 62 61 73 65 01 FF  48 00 00 00 69 00 00 00  FF FF FF FF FF 00 00 FF  00 00 00 00 00 00 FF 80
  03 00 74 6F 70 00 80  20 00 00 00 58 00 00 00  00 00 00 00 00 FF 00 FF  00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
  A test must assert: write(frame) == these 70 bytes, and read(these 70 bytes) gives the frame with layer ids 1 and 2, next_layer_id = 3.
end note

@enduml
